--- CLIPPING CENSUS (MEASURED) ---
container max   : 16383 DN. NOT the usable white level (15360) -- these are
                  two different numbers for two different purposes and both are right:
                  15360 bounds the noise model's calibrated range, 16383 is what
                  "this sample is pinned" means. Do not unify them.
ever clipped    : 0.0000% of pixels (0 of 8241504) clipped in at least one frame
always clipped  : 0.0000% of pixels (0 of 8241504) pinned in EVERY frame
                  No pixel is pinned in every frame, so the maximum-severity case
                  M26 measured on coffee-bubbles does not arise on this stack.
                  NOTE 109MSDCF and 119MSDCF are two of the four stacks with NO
                  saturation, and 109 is also the quietest photometrically (M24).
                  A clean result on them is systematically weaker evidence than it
                  looks.

--- PHOTOMETRIC DRIFT SENSITIVITY (DERIVED from a MEASURED response) ---
winner response : median 1.0721, p10 0.9409, p90 7.1353  (regularised, DN-normalised)
gate unit       : 0.021516  = sqrt(2) * FOCUS_NOISE_SD, the SD of a difference
sensitivity     : 0.249 gate units per 1% of per-frame level drift (median pixel),
                  0.219 at p10 and 1.658 at p90. Shot-limited; in read-noise-
                  dominated shadow it is 2x this.
corpus (M24)    : 109MSDCF drifts 0.91% -> 0.23 gate units. 119MSDCF 2.88% -> 0.72.
                  coffee-bean 11.70% -> 2.92. coffee-bubbles 8.93% -> 2.22.
                  109MSDCF is the QUIETEST stack in the corpus and is the one most
                  of this project's numbers were measured on, so a clean 109 result
                  is NOT evidence that photometric variation is handled.
STATUS          : NO per-frame gain term is fitted or applied. This merge assumes
                  constant photometry across the stack. The number above is the size
                  of that assumption, not a correction for it. Do NOT read gain from
                  EXIF to fix it: M24 measured two stacks drifting 6.84% and 8.93%
                  with CONSTANT EXIF, and coffee-bean moving only 16% of what its
                  EXIF change predicts (1.0443 measured vs 1.2800). Fit it.

flat ROI        : not requested. Pass --flat-roi X,Y,W,H for the noise invariant.
